H1901.definition:
from an unused root akin to H1897 (הָגָה);
properly, a murmur, i.e. complaint
KJV: meditation, musing.

H1902.definition:
intensive from H1897 (הָגָה);
a murmuring sound, i.e. a musical notation (probably similar to the modern affettuoso to indicate solemnity of movement); by implication, a machination
KJV: device, Higgaion, meditation, solemn sound.

H1903.definition:
of uncertain derivation;
perhaps suitable or turning
KJV: directly.

H1904.definition:
of uncertain (perhaps foreign) derivation;
Hagar, the mother of Ishmael
KJV: Hagar.

H1905.definition:
or (prolonged) הַגְרִיאxlit Hagrîʼ corrected to Hagrîyʼ; perhaps patronymically from H1904 (הָגָר);
a Hagrite or member of a certain Arabian clan
KJV: Hagarene, Hagarite, Haggeri.

H1906.definition:
for H1959 (הֵידָד);
a shout
KJV: sounding again.

H1907.definition:
(Aramaic) probably of foreign origin;
a vizier
KJV: counsellor.

H1908.definition:
probably of foreign origin (compare H111 (אֲדַד));
Hadad, the name of an idol, and of several kings of Edom
KJV: Hadad.

H1909.definition:
from H1908 (הֲדַד) and H5828 (עֵזֶר); Hadad (is his) help;
Hadadezer, a Syrian king
KJV: Hadadezer. Compare H1928 (הֲדַרְעֶזֶר).

H1910.definition:
from H1908 (הֲדַד) and H7417 (רִמּוֹן);
Hadad-Rimmon, a place in Palestine
KJV: Hadad-rimmon.

H1911.definition:
a primitive root (compare H3034 (יָדָה));
to stretch forth the hand
KJV: put.

H1912.definition:
of foreign origin;
Hodu (i.e. Hindustan)
KJV: India.

H1913.definition:
or הֲדֹרָם; probably of foreign derivation;
Hadoram, a son of Joktan, and the tribe descended from him
KJV: Hadoram.

H1914.definition:
of uncertain derivation;
Hiddai, an Israelite
KJV: Hiddai.

H1915.definition:
a primitive root (compare H1854 (דָּקַק));
to crush with the foot
KJV: tread down.

H1916.definition:
from an unused root meaning to stamp upon;
a foot stool
KJV: (foot-) stool.

H1917.definition:
(Aramaic) from a root corresponding to that of H1916 (הֲדֹם);
something stamped to pieces, i.e. a bit
KJV: piece.

H1918.definition:
of uncertain derivation;
the myrtle
KJV: myrtle (tree).

H1919.definition:
feminine of H1918 (הֲדַס);
Hadassah (or Esther)
KJV: Hadassah.

H1920.definition:
a primitive root;
to push away or down
KJV: cast away (out), drive, expel, thrust (away).

H1921.definition:
a primitive root;
to swell up (literally or figuratively, active or passive); by implication, to favor or honour, be high or proud
KJV: countenance, crooked place, glorious, honour, put forth.

H1922.definition:
(Aramaic) corresponding to H1921 (הָדַר);
to magnify (figuratively)
KJV: glorify, honour.

H1923.definition:
(Aramaic) from H1922 (הֲדַר)lemma הֲדַּר extra dagesh, corrected to הֲדַר;
magnificence
KJV: honour, majesty.

H1924.definition:
the same as H1926 (הָדָר);
Hadar, an Edomite
KJV: Hadar.

H1925.definition:
from H1921 (הָדַר);
honour; used (figuratively) for the capital city (Jerusalem)
KJV: glory.

H1926.definition:
from H1921 (הָדַר);
magnificence, i.e. ornament or splendor
KJV: beauty, comeliness, excellency, glorious, glory, goodly, honour, majesty.

H1927.definition:
feminine of H1926 (הָדָר);
decoration
KJV: beauty, honour.

H1928.definition:
from H1924 (הֲדַר) and H5828 (עֵזֶר); Hadar (i.e. Hadad, H1908 (הֲדַד)) is his help; (i.e. Hadadezer, H1909 (הֲדַדְעֶזֶר))
Hadarezer,  a Syrian king
KJV: Hadarezer.

H1929.definition:
a shortened form of H162 (אֲהָהּ);
ah! expressing grief
KJV: woe worth.

H1930.definition:
by permutation from H1929 (הָהּ);
oh!
KJV: alas.

H1931.definition:
of which the feminine (beyond the Pentateuch) is הִיא; a primitive word, the third person pronoun singular;
he (she or it); only expressed when emphatic or without a verb; also (intensively) self, or (especially with the article) the same; sometimes (as demonstrative) this or that; occasionally (instead of copula) as or are
KJV: he, as for her, him(-self), it, the same, she (herself), such, that (...it), these, they, this, those, which (is), who.

H1932.definition:
(Aramaic) or (feminine) הִיא; (Aramaic), corresponding to H1931 (הוּא)
{he (she or it); self, or (especially with the article) the same; sometimes (as demonstrative) this or that; occasionally (instead of copula) as or are}
KJV: [idiom] are, it, this.

H1933.definition:
or הָוָה; a primitive root (compare H183 (אָוָה), H1961 (הָיָה)) supposed to mean properly, to breathe;
to be (in the sense of existence)
KJV: be, [idiom] have.

H1934.definition:
(Aramaic) or הָוָה; (Aramaic), corresponding to H1933 (הָוָא);
to exist; used in a great variety of applications (especially in connection with other words)
KJV: be, become, [phrase] behold, [phrase] came (to pass), [phrase] cease, [phrase] cleave, [phrase] consider, [phrase] do, [phrase] give, [phrase] have, [phrase] judge, [phrase] keep, [phrase] labour, [phrase] mingle (self), [phrase] put, [phrase] see, [phrase] seek, [phrase] set, [phrase] slay, [phrase] take heed, tremble, [phrase] walk, [phrase] would.

H1935.definition:
from an unused root;
grandeur (i.e. an imposing form and appearance)
KJV: beauty, comeliness, excellency, glorious, glory, goodly, honour, majesty.

H1936.definition:
the same as H1935 (הוֹד);
Hod, an Israelite
KJV: Hod.

H1937.definition:
a form of H1938 (הוֹדַוְיָה);
Hodevah (or Hodevjah), an Israelite
KJV: Hodevah.

H1938.definition:
from H1935 (הוֹד) and H3050 (יָהּ); majesty of Jah;
Hodavjah, the name of three Israelites
KJV: Hodaviah.

H1939.definition:
a form of H1938 (הוֹדַוְיָה);
Hodajvah, an Israelite
KJV: Hodaiah.

H1940.definition:
a form for the feminine of H3064 (יְהוּדִי);
a Jewess
KJV: Hodiah.

H1941.definition:
a form of H1938 (הוֹדַוְיָה);
Hodijah, the name of three Israelites
KJV: Hodijah.

H1942.definition:
from H1933 (הָוָא) (in the sense of eagerly coveting and rushing upon;
by implication, of falling); desire; also ruin
KJV: calamity, iniquity, mischief, mischievous (thing), naughtiness, naughty, noisome, perverse thing, substance, very wickedness.

H1943.definition:
another form for H1942 (הַוָּה);
ruin
KJV: mischief.

H1944.definition:
of uncertain derivation;
Hoham, a Canaanitish king
KJV: Hoham.

H1945.definition:
a prolonged form of H1930 (הוֹ) (akin to H188 (אוֹי));
oh!
KJV: ah, alas, ho, O, woe.

H1946.definition:
(Aramaic) corresponding to H1981 (הֲלַךְ);
to go; causatively, to bring
KJV: bring again, come, go (up).

H1947.definition:
feminine active participle of H1984 (הָלַל);
folly
KJV: madness.

H1948.definition:
from active participle of H1984 (הָלַל);
folly
KJV: madness.

H1949.definition:
a primitive root (compare H2000 (הָמַם));
to make an uproar, or agitate greatly
KJV: destroy, move, make a noise, put, ring again.

H1950.definition:
from H2000 (הָמַם); raging;
Homam, an Edomitish chieftain
KJV: Homam. Compare H1967 (הֵימָם).

H1951.definition:
a primitive root;
properly, to be naught, i.e. (figuratively) to be (causatively, act) light
KJV: be ready.

H1952.definition:
from the same as H1951 (הוּן) in the sense of H202 (אוֹן);
wealth; by implication, enough
KJV: enough, [phrase] for nought, riches, substance, wealth.

H1953.definition:
from H3068 (יְהֹוָה) and H8085 (שָׁמַע); Jehovah has heard;
Hoshama, an Israelite
KJV: Hoshama.

H1954.definition:
from H3467 (יָשַׁע); deliverer;
Hoshea, the name of five Israelites
KJV: Hosea, Hoshea, Oshea.

H1955.definition:
from H3467 (יָשַׁע) and H3050 (יָהּ); Jah has saved;
Hoshajah, the name of two Israelites
KJV: Hoshaiah.

H1956.definition:
from H3498 (יָתַר); he has caused to remain;
Hothir, an Israelite
KJV: Hothir.

H1957.definition:
a primitive root (compare H2372 (חָזָה));
to dream
KJV: sleep.

H1958.definition:
for H5092 (נְהִי);
lamentation
KJV: woe. (For hiyr. See H1931 (הוּא), H1932 (הוּא).)

H1959.definition:
from an unused root (meaning to shout);
acclamation
KJV: shout(-ing).

H1960.definition:
from the same as H1959 (הֵידָד);
properly, an acclaim, i.e. a choir of singers
KJV: thanksgiving.

H1961.definition:
a primitive root (compare H1933 (הָוָא));
to exist, i.e. be or become, come to pass (always emphatic, and not a mere copula or auxiliary)
KJV: beacon, [idiom] altogether, be(-come), accomplished, committed, like), break, cause, come (to pass), do, faint, fall, [phrase] follow, happen, [idiom] have, last, pertain, quit (one-) self, require, [idiom] use.

H1962.definition:
another form for H1943 (הֹוָה);
ruin
KJV: calamity.

H1963.definition:
another form for H349 (אֵיךְ);
how?
KJV: how.

H1964.definition:
probably from H3201 (יָכֹל) (in the sense of capacity);
a large public building, such as a palace or temple
KJV: palace, temple.

H1965.definition:
(Aramaic) corresponding to H1964 (הֵיכָל)
{a large public building, such as a palace or temple}
KJV: palace, temple.

H1966.definition:
from H1984 (הָלַל) (in the sense of brightness);
the morning-star
KJV: lucifer.

H1967.definition:
another form for H1950 (הוֹמָם);
Hemam, an Idumaean
KJV: Hemam.

H1968.definition:
probably from H539 (אָמַן); faithful;
Heman, the name of at least two Israelites
KJV: Heman.

H1969.definition:
probably of Egyptian origin;
a hin or liquid measure
KJV: hin.

H1971.definition:
from H5234 (נָכַר);
respect, i.e. partiality
KJV: shew.

H1972.definition:
probably denominatively from H1973 (הָלְאָה)xlit hâlᵉâh corrected to hâlᵉʼâh;
to remove or be remote
KJV: cast far off.

H1973.definition:
from the primitive form of the article (hal);
to the distance, i.e. far away; also (of time) thus far
KJV: back, beyond, (hence,-) forward, hitherto, thence, forth, yonder.

H1974.definition:
from H1984 (הָלַל) (in the sense of rejoicing);
a celebration of thanksgiving for harvest
KJV: merry, praise.

H1975.definition:
from H1976 (הַלָּזֶה);
this or that
KJV: side, that, this.

H1976.definition:
from the article (see H1973 (הָלְאָה)xlit hâlᵉâh corrected to hâlᵉʼâh) and H2088 (זֶה);
this very
KJV: this.

H1977.definition:
another form of H1976 (הַלָּזֶה);
that
KJV: this.

H1978.definition:
from H1980 (הָלַךְ);
a walk, i.e. (by implication) a step
KJV: step.

H1979.definition:
feminine of H1978 (הָלִיךְ);
a walking; by implication, a procession or march, a caravan
KJV: company, going, walk, way.

H1980.definition:
akin to H3212 (יָלַךְ); a primitive root;
to walk (in a great variety of applications, literally and figuratively)
KJV: (all) along, apace, behave (self), come, (on) continually, be conversant, depart, [phrase] be eased, enter, exercise (self), [phrase] follow, forth, forward, get, go (about, abroad, along, away, forward, on, out, up and down), [phrase] greater, grow, be wont to haunt, lead, march, [idiom] more and more, move (self), needs, on, pass (away), be at the point, quite, run (along), [phrase] send, speedily, spread, still, surely, [phrase] tale-bearer, [phrase] travel(-ler), walk (abroad, on, to and fro, up and down, to places), wander, wax, (way-) faring man, [idiom] be weak, whirl.

H1981.definition:
(Aramaic) corresponding to H1980 (הָלַךְ) (compare H1946 (הוּךְ));
to walk
KJV: walk.

H1982.definition:
from H1980 (הָלַךְ);
properly, a journey, i.e. (by implication) a wayfarer; also a flowing
KJV: [idiom] dropped, traveller.

H1983.definition:
(Aramaic) from H1981 (הֲלַךְ);
properly, a journey, i.e. (by implication) toll on goods at aroad
KJV: custom.

H1984.definition:
a primitive root;
to be clear (orig. of sound, but usually of color); to shine; hence, to make ashow, to boast; and thus to be (clamorously) foolish; to rave; causatively, to celebrate; also to stultify
KJV: (make) boast (self), celebrate, commend, (deal, make), fool(-ish, -ly), glory, give (light), be (make, feign self) mad (against), give in marriage, (sing, be worthy of) praise, rage, renowned, shine.

H1985.definition:
from H1984 (הָלַל); praising (namely God);
Hillel, an Israelite
KJV: Hillel.

H1986.definition:
a primitive root;
to strike down; by implication, to hammer, stamp, conquer, disband
KJV: beat (down), break (down), overcome, smite (with the hammer).

H1987.definition:
from H1986 (הָלַם); smiter;
Helem, the name of two Israelites
KJV: Helem.

H1988.definition:
from the article (see H1973 (הָלְאָה)xlit hâlᵉâh corrected to hâlᵉʼâh);
hither
KJV: here, hither(-(to)), thither.

H1989.definition:
from H1986 (הָלַם);
a hammer (or mallet)
KJV: hammer.

H1990.definition:
of uncertain derivation;
Ham, a region of Palestine
KJV: Ham.

H1991.definition:
from H1993 (הָמָה);
abundance, i.e. wealth
KJV: any of theirs.

H1992.definition:
or (prolonged) הֵמָּה; masculine plural from H1981 (הֲלַךְ);
they (only used when emphatic)
KJV: it, like, [idiom] (how, so) many (soever, more as) they (be), (the) same, [idiom] so, [idiom] such, their, them, these, they, those, which, who, whom, withal, ye.

H1993.definition:
a primitive root (compare H1949 (הוּם));
to make a loud sound (like English 'hum'); by implication, to be in great commotion or tumult, to rage, war, moan, clamor
KJV: clamorous, concourse, cry aloud, be disquieted, loud, mourn, be moved, make a noise, rage, roar, sound, be troubled, make in tumult, tumultuous, be in an uproar.

H1994.definition:
(Aramaic) or (prolonged) הִמּוֹן; (Aramaic), corresponding to H1992 (הֵם);
they
KJV: [idiom] are, them, those.

H1995.definition:
or הָמֹן; (Ezekiel 5:7), from H1993 (הָמָה);
a noise, tumult, crowd; also disquietude, wealth
KJV: abundance, company, many, multitude, multiply, noise, riches, rumbling, sounding, store, tumult.

H1996.definition:
from H1995 (הָמוֹן) and H1463 (גּוֹג);
the multitude of Gog; the fanciful name of an emblematic place in Palestine
KJV: Hamogog.

H1999.definition:
or (too fully) הֲמוּלָּה; (Jeremiah 11:16), feminine passive participle of an unused root meaning to rush (as rain with a windy roar);
a sound
KJV: speech, tumult.
